{
  "id": "cultural-process",
  "term": "cultural process",
  "definition": "A cultural process is a patterned way that thinking and action are shaped through shared, culturally learned systems such as ways of sensing, attending, remembering, and responding. In this sense, behavior is not created from nothing, but emerges by reorganizing embodied experience within a common cultural framework.",
